---
title: "publish_transaction (Sui Whitepaper: Package Publishing)"
---
stateDiagram-v2
    direction TB
    [*] --> q_receive: receive Publish transaction containing Package
    q_receive --> q_verify: run Move bytecode verifier on each module in Package

    q_verify --> q_link: bytecode verification passes
    q_verify --> q_error_verify: verification fails (type/memory/resource safety violation)
    q_error_verify --> [*]: return error

    q_link --> q_check_deps: link package against dependencies (list of ObjRef to published packages)
    q_check_deps --> q_run_init: all dependencies resolved and valid
    q_check_deps --> q_error_deps: dependency resolution failed
    q_error_deps --> [*]: return error

    q_run_init --> q_init_iter: for each module in package
    q_init_iter --> q_run_module_init: run module initializer
    q_run_module_init --> q_init_iter: more modules remaining
    q_run_module_init --> q_create_pkg_obj: all initializers complete

    q_create_pkg_obj --> q_store: create Package object (immutable, read-only)
    q_store --> [*]: package object stored in global pool as read-only

    note right of q_verify
        INV-001: Bytecode verifier ensures type safety, memory safety, resource safety
        INV-002: Published packages are read-only objects (cannot be mutated or deleted)
        INV-003: Module initializers bootstrap initial application state
        INV-004: Modules can import types and invoke functions from other modules
    end note
